# Leaks LeakSanitizer reports that are not leaks of the client's, each
# matched as narrowly as the stacks allow, with why.

# An image still loading when the app tests exit: Qt's pixmap reader has
# stopped by then, so the response's cancel is never answered with its
# deletion. The provider goes with it, kept alive by the response.
leak:Artwork::requestImageResponse

# mpv's built-in Lua scripts (Ubuntu's libmpv links Lua 5.2), mid-allocation
# when a test exits before the probe in MpvFacts::ask is terminated. Matched
# on Lua, not on libmpv, so an mpv handle the client fails to destroy is
# still reported.
leak:liblua5.2.so
